!-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Biomass-burning surface emissions (GFED NRT, PD/2025 -- per MMPPE.md's
! "Biomass burning emission: GFED5.1 (daily) for PD" and general forcing
! datasets note). Source data regridded to f09 in
! /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/. Pointed at the
! 2025 file (not 2024/2026) and cycled on that single year so the 3-month
! spin-up (and any OAT run that reuses this block) loops it cyclically
! rather than running off the end of a single calendar year.
!
! GFED ships raw species (BC, OC, SO2, C2H6S); CAM6's MAM4 chemistry needs
! them re-expressed as bc_a4/pom_a4/SO2/so4_a1/DMS + num_a4/num_a1 (MAM4 has
! no bare "BC"/"OC" tracer). That conversion -- OC -> pom_a4 = 1.4*OC (OM/OC
! ratio), SO2 -> {SO2 = 0.975*SO2_raw, so4_a1 = 0.025*SO2_raw} (primary-
! sulfate split, conserves total biomass-burning sulfur), BC -> bc_a4 and
! C2H6S -> DMS (rename only, no scaling), plus num_bc_a4/num_pom_a4/
! num_so4_a1 companion number-emission files -- is done by
! forcing_datasets/derive_gfed_mam4_speciation.py, which documents every
! constant/formula in detail (citing
! /glade/u/home/bduran/multimodel-erfaci/diagnostics/redistribute_emiss_hires.ncl,
! the ACOM reference script these conventions come from) and writes its
! output back into forcing_datasets/regridded/. Read that script's
! docstring before touching any of the GFED-derived filenames below --
! notably, num_pom_a4 is intentionally derived from RAW (unscaled) OC mass,
! not the 1.4x pom_a4 mass, which looks like a bug but matches the
! reference convention exactly (explained there).
!
! srf_emis_specifier targets below use "*_bb_*"-tagged SYMLINKS/files for
! the real regridded/derived files, not un-tagged filenames: this branch's
! mo_srf_emissions.F90 (get_srf_emis_ppe_scale) only applies the
! emi_bb_bc/emi_bb_oc/emi_bb_so2 PPE scale factors when the emission
! filename contains "_bb_" (see ppe_changes_incorporated.txt, 6b). The
! as-regridded GFED filenames (emiss_GFED_NRT_<SPECIES>_wildfire_2025_...)
! don't contain that tag, which would silently leave those three knobs
! inert once perturbed in the later OAT runs even though this CTL run
! (all scale factors at their default of 1.0) is unaffected either way.
! Harmless no-op for THIS file; load-bearing for the emi_bb_bc/oc/so2 OAT
! parameter_L/H runs that get initialized from this spin-up. so4_a1/num_a1
! have no PPE scale-factor case in get_srf_emis_ppe_scale() at all (same as
! the CEDS anthro so4_a1/num_a1 entries further below), so the "_bb_" tag is
! moot for them specifically -- included anyway for naming consistency with
! the rest of this file set.
!
! UNITS FIX: the regridded GFED/BB4CMIP7 files carry units="kg m-2 s-1"
! (CF/input4MIPs convention), which did NOT match mo_srf_emissions.F90's
! mks_units whitelist (only slash-delimited variants: "kg/m2/s" etc) --
! that would have silently sent these files down the molecules/cm2/s
! branch and scaled true mass flux by amufac*mw (~1e-22), i.e. read as
! ~zero. Fixed by adding "kg m-2 s-1" to mks_units in mo_srf_emissions.F90
! directly (so any correctly CF-labeled file works without renaming/
! recopying). Re-run case.build after any fresh checkout of this branch to
! pick up that source change. This fix also covers the new so4_a1_bb/
! num_so4_a1_bb files below (same units convention).
!
! num_a4/num_a1 (companion number-emission flux for bc_a4/pom_a4/so4_a1
! biomass burning): derived from the GFED BC/OC/so4_a1 mass flux via
! num_flux = mass_flux_kg_m2_s / (amufac * rho*(pi/6)*diam^3), the same
! formula/assumed particle size (diam=0.134e-6 m, matching this branch's
! fire_emissions.F90 demis_acc constant) as ACOM's
! redistribute_emiss_hires.ncl (see derive_gfed_mam4_speciation.py
! docstring for the full derivation and the num_pom_a4 raw-vs-scaled-OC
! caveat noted above) -- validated by reproducing the pre-existing
! num_bc_a4_bb/num_pom_a4_bb files' embedded formula constants exactly.
! emi_cmr_bb (the PPE knob that would otherwise let CAM derive number from
! mass at runtime) is still not implemented (ppe_changes_incorporated.txt,
! 6c), so this is a static, unperturbable number-emission dataset
! consistent with this CTL run's all-defaults state -- revisit if
! emi_cmr_bb is ever implemented.
!
! Anthropogenic surface emissions (CEDS CMIP7, PD/2025 -- per MMPPE.md's
! anthropogenic emissions requirement). Source: CMIP7 input4MIPs CEDS
! release at /glade/campaign/acom/MUSICA/emis/cmip7/f09/CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18
! (f09, monthly, 1750-2023, molecules cm-2 s-1 -- matches this branch's
! normal unit-handling path, no fix needed like the regridded GFED files
! above). srf_emis_type/srf_emis_cycle_yr above (CYCLICAL/2025) apply
! globally to the whole srf_emis_specifier list, so these files get the
! same "read year 2025, cycle it" treatment as the bb entries.
!
! YEAR MISMATCH, FIXED (2026-08-07): the CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18 release only
! actually contains data through 2023-12 (verified via ncdump on every file
! below -- "date" never exceeds 20231216, despite the "175001-202312"
! filename-embedded range suggesting otherwise once you'd expect a 2025
! extension; real CEDS releases run ~2 years behind). srf_emis_cycle_yr=2025
! against a file with no 2025 "date" record hard-crashes
! (tracer_data.F90:set_cycle_indices(), 'cycle year not found') -- this
! would have crashed EVERY anthropogenic-emissions file below (and the two
! CEDS "ene_vertical" ext_frc entries further down) the moment this CTL run
! started. Per bduran's request (2026-08-07), all 13 affected CEDS files are
! now pointed at forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/ copies in which the
! last real year (2023) is repeated unchanged as BOTH 2024 and 2025 (24
! monthly records instead of the source's 3288) -- produced by
! forcing_datasets/relabel_2025_climo.py's relabel_ceds(), which also
! documents this in each output file's "history_relabel" attribute. This is
! a modeling approximation (2023 anthropogenic activity standing in for
! 2025), not a pure bookkeeping fix like the H2O/contvolcano relabeling
! below -- flag it as such in any run documentation. Repeating 2024 as well
! (not just 2025) means these same files will also work unmodified for a
! future transient SERIAL run spanning 2024-2025 (see the "FUTURE PPE RUNS"
! note further below), without needing to be regenerated again once real
! CEDS 2024/2025 data ships.
!
! Limited to species where F2000climo's default (2000_cam6.xml) already
! specifies an "anthro" source and a CEDS CMIP7 file (or pair of files)
! maps cleanly onto it:
!   bc_a4, pom_a4              <- single CEDS "-em-anthro" file (all anthro
!                                  sectors aggregated), 1-to-1 vs. default's
!                                  single anthro surface file.
!   num_a4 (x2)                <- ditto, independently-tracked number-
!                                  emission datasets for bc_a4/pom_a4.
!   SOAG                       <- CEDS SOAGx1.5-VOC-anthro (see below),
!                                  matching F2000climo's use of the x1.5-
!                                  scaled SOAG anthro dataset.
!   so4_a1, num_a1 (x2)        <- CEDS splits these into a surface component
!                                  (ag[+ship_slv], matching default's
!                                  "anthro-ag-ship") and an elevated
!                                  energy-sector component (ene_vertical,
!                                  matching default's "anthro-ene" -- see
!                                  ext_frc_specifier below). num_a1 has two
!                                  separate CEDS surface files (ag, ship_slv)
!                                  where CMIP6/default combined them into one.
!   so4_a2, num_a2              <- CEDS res_trs (Transportation+Residential),
!                                  matching default's single "anthro-res"
!                                  surface file.
!   SO2                         <- CEDS SO2-em-anthro -- SEE CAVEAT BELOW,
!                                  this one is NOT a clean 1-to-1 map.
! NH3 was considered and dropped: no default srf_emis entry in 2000_cam6.xml,
! and not even a solution-class species in this compset's chemistry
! mechanism (src/chemistry/pp_trop_mam4/chem_mech.in) -- an NH3 emission
! entry would be a no-op at best.
!
! SO2 CAVEAT -- vertical placement changes vs. the default: F2000climo's
! default splits anthropogenic SO2 into a surface component
! (anthro-ag-ship-res, srf_emis) and an elevated energy-sector component
! (anthro-ene, ext_frc), the same way it does for so4_a1/num_a1. CEDS7 does
! NOT provide that split for SO2 -- SO2-em-anthro is a single file with all
! anthro sectors (including Energy) already summed into one all-surface
! field (checked both cmip7/f09/CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18/ and the sibling
! .../CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18_20251124/ release -- identical in this respect,
! same creation_date, just repackaged with a newer timestamp; the only
! genuinely new thing in the _20251124 directory is an unrelated
! "-em-AIR-anthro" aircraft sector for bc_a4/CO/NO2/num_bc_a4/SO2, a 4D
! altitude-resolved forcing CAM's tracer_data.F90 can actually ingest --
! it auto-detects an 'altitude'/'altitude_int' km grid as an alternative to
! the legacy 'lev' hPa convention, ~line 331-377 -- but that's an
! additional emissions category outside F2000climo's default, not a fix
! for this gap, and that directory is also missing SOAG/SOAGx1.5 entirely;
! left out of this round by request).
!
! Given no CEDS7 release splits SO2 by sector, wired the whole
! SO2-em-anthro file into srf_emis_specifier below (energy-sector SO2 now
! emitted at the surface instead of aloft, unlike so4_a1/num_a1's ene_
! vertical component in ext_frc_specifier) rather than leave anthropogenic
! SO2 out entirely.
!
! SOAG file choice: CEDS provides two SOAGx1.5-VOC-anthro files with
! identical data_creator/creation_date (20260122) but the un-suffixed one
! (...supplemental_gn_175001-202312.nc) has NO "date" variable, only a raw
! CF "time" coordinate -- tracer_data.F90's open_trc_datafile()/
! set_cycle_indices() unconditionally look up a variable literally named
! "date" (YYYYMMDD int) to do CYCLICAL year-matching, so that file would
! fail to load. The "_c20260122" suffixed twin has the required "date"
! variable added and is what's used below. Checked (ncdump -h, grep
! "date(time)") that every other CEDS file referenced in this namelist has
! it too before wiring each one in.
!
! PPE note: get_srf_emis_ppe_scale() (mo_srf_emissions.F90) matches the
! emi_anthro_bc/emi_anthro_oc/emi_anthro_so2 scale-factor knobs by looking
! for the literal substring "anthro" in the filename (and, for num_a4, also
! "bc_a4" or "pom_a4" to pick the right parent-species scale) -- these CEDS
! filenames satisfy both naturally, no renaming/symlinking needed here
! (unlike the "_bb_" tag required for the GFED biomass-burning files
! above). This applies to the new SO2-em-anthro entry too: SO2 already had
! a PPE scale case (srf_emis_scale_so2_ant/so2_bb) for the bb entry above,
! so the anthro entry picks up srf_emis_scale_so2_ant automatically --
! meaning that knob will now perturb the FULL anthropogenic SO2 field
! (including the energy-sector portion that's normally split out via
! ext_frc for so4_a1/num_a1), not just a surface-only subset, per the
! caveat above. so4_a1, so4_a2, num_a1, num_a2, and SOAG have no PPE
! scale-factor case in get_srf_emis_ppe_scale() at all, so this is moot for
! them (scale stays at its default of 1.0 regardless of filename).
!
! Prescribed ozone (CMIP7 ScenarioMIP "vl", PD/2025 -- per MMPPE.md).
! prescribed_ozone_* below (in &chem_inparm) replaces F2000climo's default
! (2000_cam6.xml's ozone_strataero_CAM6chem_2000climo_zm_5day_c171004.nc).
! That default file is CAM history output repurposed as a zonal-mean,
! hybrid-sigma-pressure prescribed_ozone/prescribed_strataero source; the
! reader only actually needs O3(time,lev,lat) + date (no lon, no PS/hyam/
! hybm required -- see forcing_datasets/reformat_ozone_zonal_mean.py's
! docstring for the full derivation of what tracer_data.F90 requires).
!
! The regridded CEDS/ScenarioMIP ozone file has vertical dim "plev"
! (descending, pure pressure, 4D with lon) -- this branch's tracer_data.F90
! hardcodes a lookup for a dimension literally named "lev" (ascending), so
! it can't be used directly. forcing_datasets/reformat_ozone_zonal_mean.py
! zonal-averages over lon, reverses+renames plev->lev, renames vmro3->O3
! (units set to the exact string "mol/mol" -- the source's CF "mole mole-1"
! is not one of the unit strings prescribed_ozone_adv() recognizes and
! would hard-error at runtime), and adds the date/datesec variables
! open_trc_datafile() requires (derived from the source's CF time
! coordinate; not present in the source file). Output:
! forcing_datasets/regridded/ozone_zm_input4MIPs_ScenarioMIP_FZJ-CMIP-
! ozone-vl-1-0_0.9x1.25_202401-202612.nc.
!
! CYCLICAL/cycle_yr=2025 below matches every other forcing source in this
! file (GHG, GFED, CEDS anthro, ext_frc, nudging) -- all PD/2025-
! representative for the CTL spin-up and OAT runs. The output file covers
! 2024-01 through 2026-12 (all 36 months kept, not trimmed to 2025 alone --
! same PD_WINDOW buffer rationale as the other CEDS/GFED files in this set)
! but only the 2025 slice is ever looked up under CYCLICAL.
!
! FUTURE PPE RUNS, NOT THIS FILE: transient PPE runs starting in 2024 and
! running through 2025 will need prescribed_ozone_type='SERIAL' instead of
! 'CYCLICAL' (and probably drop prescribed_ozone_cycle_yr entirely) so CAM
! reads forward through the real 2024-2026 monthly data rather than
! re-cycling one year -- per bduran's request (2026-08-06), left as a
! future change, not implemented here.
!
! NOT YET INCLUDED (known gaps, not resolved this round):
!   - Aircraft ("AIR"-sector) emissions -- see SO2 caveat above.
!   - SST/SIC (ERA5 2025) forcing: a data-ocean/ice
!     (user_nl_docn/SSTICE_DATA_FILENAME) setting, not a user_nl_cam one,
!     and out of scope for this file.
!-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Elevated (ext_frc) emissions (see ext_frc_specifier below). Was previously
! left unset here (so this case ran on 2000_cam6.xml's full CMIP6 default:
! H2O CH4-oxidation source + num_a1/so4_a1 anthro-ene (elevated energy-
! sector) + 5 contvolcano (continuous volcanic SO2/sulfate) lines, all at
! cycle_yr=2000). Now overridden to swap the anthro-ene lines for their
! CEDS CMIP7 "ene_vertical" equivalents (matching the so4_a1/num_a1
! srf_emis CEDS swap below); H2O is carried forward from the same 2000climo
! source as the default, but the 5 contvolcano lines are sourced from 1850
! conditions instead of 2000 (see below), per bduran's request.
!
! ext_frc_specifier is a single global list -- setting it here REPLACES the
! full use_case default, it does not append to it. Omitting the H2O/
! contvolcano lines would silently drop CH4-oxidation water vapor and
! volcanic SO2/sulfate forcing from the run, so they're carried forward
! explicitly below.
!
! CONTVOLCANO SOURCE -- 1850, not 2000: the 5 contvolcano lines below (num_a1/
! num_a2/SO2/so4_a1/so4_a2) are sourced from year 1850 of
! .../CMIP6_emissions_1750_2015/emissions-cmip6_*_contvolcano_vertical_850-5000_...
! -- the exact same files namelist_defaults_cam.xml's ver="cam6" default
! points at (so2_cv_ext_file etc., ~line 758-762), i.e. what CESM's own
! official 1850_cam6.xml use case uses for continuous-volcano forcing, NOT
! the "2000climo" files 2000_cam6.xml (F2000climo's default) points at. Per
! bduran's request (2026-08-06): use 1850 (CMIP6 preindustrial/background)
! volcanic conditions for this run rather than year-2000 conditions -- "that
! is what is done in CMIP6". The "_850-5000_" files aren't a continuous
! transient record despite the name: each holds exactly 7 embedded 12-month
! climatological blocks (years 850, 1850, 1960, 2000, 2005, 2010, 5000);
! 1850's block is real source data, sliced out (not extrapolated) before
! relabeling. See forcing_datasets/relabel_2025_climo.py's docstring for
! the full derivation.
!
! YEAR MISMATCH / RELABELED FILES: ext_frc_type/ext_frc_cycle_yr are global
! scalars applied to every file in ext_frc_specifier (same architecture as
! srf_emis above) -- tracer_data.F90's set_cycle_indices() hard-errors
! (call endrun('cycle year not found')) if the requested cycle_yr isn't
! present in a file's "date" variable. Neither the H2O 2000climo file nor
! the volcano files' 1850 block contain a 2025 date -- so ext_frc_cycle_yr=
! 2025 (wanted for the CEDS files, to match srf_emis_cycle_yr above) would
! crash on them as-is.
!
! Fixed by making local copies with ONLY the "date" variable's year shifted
! to 2025 (H2O: 2000->2025, date+250000; contvolcano: 1850->2025, date+
! 1750000; all other data byte-identical to the source -- verified via
! netCDF4 max-abs-diff: 0.0, both for H2O's CH4_CHML field and the volcano
! files' contvolcano/PS fields against the source's own 1850 block). This is
! safe because tracer_data.F90 builds its internal time axis purely from
! "date"/"datesec" (see open_trc_datafile(), ~line 1925-1929) and never
! reads the files' own CF "time" coordinate for this purpose -- so
! relabeling "date" alone is sufficient, and "time" is left as the source's
! original values (not reset to start at record 0) for both categories.
!   - Script:  forcing_datasets/relabel_2025_climo.py
!   - Output:  forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/  (6 files: H2O +
!              5 contvolcano; num_a1/so4_a1 anthro-ene were dropped instead
!              of relabeled since CEDS already replaces them)
!   - Each output file carries a "history_relabel" global attribute noting
!     the shift/slice and the reason.
!
! Both srf_emis_* and ext_frc_* live in this one &chem_inparm block
! deliberately -- Fortran namelists don't reliably support the same group
! name appearing twice in one file, so everything chem_inparm-related for
! this case is kept in a single group below.
!-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
&chem_inparm
 srf_emis_type      = 'CYCLICAL'
 srf_emis_cycle_yr  = 2025
 srf_emis_specifier = 'bc_a4  -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_BC_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'pom_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_pom_a4_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'SO2    -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_SO2_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'DMS    -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_C2H6S_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'num_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_num_bc_a4_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'num_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_num_pom_a4_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'so4_a1 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_so4_a1_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'num_a1 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/regridded/emiss_GFED_NRT_num_so4_a1_bb_wildfire_2025_r1440x720_0.9x1.25_202501-202512.nc',
      'bc_a4  -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/bc_a4-em-anthro_input4MIPs_emissions_CMIP_CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18_gn_2024-2025climo.nc',
      'pom_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/pom_a4-em-anthro_input4MIPs_emissions_CMIP_CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18_gn_2024-2025climo.nc',
      'num_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/num_bc_a4-em-anthro_input4MIPs_emissions_CMIP_CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18_gn_2024-2025climo.nc',
      'num_a4 -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/num_pom_a4-em-anthro_input4MIPs_emissions_CMIP_CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18_gn_2024-2025climo.nc',
      'SOAG   -> /glade/work/bduran/clean-CAM/forcing_datasets/relabeled_2025_climo/SOAGx1.5-VOC-anthro_input4MIPs_emissions_CMIP_CEDS-CMIP-2025-04-18-supplemental_gn_2024-2025climo_c20260122.nc',
